note Translation of Erlang/OTP calendar.erl offset_string_adjustment/3

choice OffsetError
    BadOffset
    note WORKAROUND: Erlang raises a badmatch or case_clause exception when Tz is malformed (too short, bad sign, bad separator) and badarg from list_to_integer on non-digits; Scribe needs every failure named, so the distinct crashes collapse into one invented BadOffset

to parse_int text
    given text is Text
    produces an Int
    fails with NotANumber
    note list_to_integer, as used in example 6 of the doc

to offset_string_adjustment time and unit for tz
    given time is an Int
    given unit is a TimeUnit
    given tz is Text
    produces an Int
    fails with BadOffset
    note UNCLEAR: time and unit are ignored by every clause; the doc does not say whether an unused parameter is allowed, warned or needs a marker like Erlang's leading underscore
    note WORKAROUND: the result is a number of seconds as a plain Int; the doc's units-in-types (example 17) would make this a Duration, but the original is unitless and the sign carries meaning, so no unit is claimed

    if tz is "Z" or tz is "z"
        give back 0

    note GAP: destructuring a string as a list of characters - Erlang matches [Sign, H1, H2 | MinutesDiff] = Tz; the doc has no list or string pattern, no character type and no substring operation, so `character i of tz` and `characters i until j of tz` are invented
    if count of tz is less than 3
        fail with BadOffset
    let sign be character 0 of tz
    let rest be characters 3 until count of tz of tz

    let hour be handle_bad_offset (characters 1 until 3 of tz)

    var minutes starts at 0
    if count of rest is 0
        set minutes to 0
    otherwise if count of rest is 3 and character 0 of rest is ":"
        set minutes to handle_bad_offset (characters 1 until 3 of rest)
    otherwise
        fail with BadOffset
    note WORKAROUND: the Erlang `case MinutesDiff of [$:, M1, M2] -> ...; [] -> 0` is a match on list shape; `choose` only matches variants and maybe values, so it becomes an if chain on length and content

    let adjustment be 3600 * hour + 60 * minutes
    if sign is "-"
        give back 0 - adjustment
        note UNCLEAR: unary minus is not shown in the doc; `0 - adjustment` is used
    otherwise if sign is "+"
        give back adjustment
    otherwise
        fail with BadOffset

to handle_bad_offset digits
    given digits is Text
    produces an Int
    fails with BadOffset
    note WORKAROUND: a helper only to turn NotANumber into BadOffset; the doc's `handle` must wrap a whole block and give back from it, so mapping one failure name to another inline needs a separate operation

    handle
        give back try parse_int digits
    on failure NotANumber
        fail with BadOffset
